Author: Dan on Selwyn <dan@awto.au>
Date:   Wed Aug 12 12:57:49 2026 +1000

    soc: retire the PMOD clock mirror, recoverable as a patch (#294)
    
    Divided copies of every clock on PMOD A, for a scope. It answered "what is the
    die actually running at" and has not been asked since.
    
    Already OFF by default, so this is not area in a shipping build. What it costs
    is the VARIANT SPACE: `mirror` and `mirrordiv` are two axes in the digest and
    in every build directory name, so the bitcache carries the cross product of two
    knobs nobody turns.
    
    Its own cost when on is not small either -- a fabric register in every mirrored
    domain, and on `hr_fast` that pulls an edge clock onto the primary network,
    which is the resource #314 is about.
    
    Restore with `git apply patches/294-clock-mirror.patch` (next commit).

